From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] users: Say when the new password is the encryption password

Plinius: pam_plinius_crypt (plinius-crypt) refuses a new login password
that opens the encrypted root, with "BAD PASSWORD: it is the encryption
password, ...". Without this the password dialog only said "Unknown
error". The text is in the plinius-control-center domain.
---
--- a/panels/system/users/run-passwd.c
+++ b/panels/system/users/run-passwd.c
@@ -421,7 +421,14 @@
                 /* Ohnoes! */
                 g_autoptr(GError) error = NULL;
 
-                if (strstr (str->str, "recovered") != NULL) {
+                /* Plinius: pam_plinius_crypt (plinius-crypt) refuses the encryption password */
+                if (strstr (str->str, "encryption password") != NULL) {
+                    error = g_error_new (PASSWD_ERROR, PASSWD_ERROR_REJECTED, "%s",
+                                         g_dgettext ("plinius-control-center",
+                                                     "The new password is the encryption password. Choose a "
+                                                     "different one, so that the PIN alone does not open the "
+                                                     "phone."));
+                } else if (strstr (str->str, "recovered") != NULL) {
                     /* What does this indicate?
                      * "Authentication information cannot be recovered?" from libpam? */
                     error = g_error_new_literal (PASSWD_ERROR, PASSWD_ERROR_UNKNOWN, str->str);
